    ($SATQ$00723d16$SATQ$, $SATQ$2b8c0dff-e373-422a-a150-3f281e461330$SATQ$::uuid, NULL, NULL, $SATQ$qbank$SATQ$, $SATQ$SAT$SATQ$, 2, $SATQ$Math$SATQ$, $SATQ$Algebra$SATQ$, $SATQ$H$SATQ$, $SATQ$H.C.$SATQ$, $SATQ$Linear equations in two variables$SATQ$, $SATQ$H$SATQ$, 6, $SATQ$spr$SATQ$, NULL, $SATQ$<p>Line&nbsp;<math alttext="script l"><mi mathvariant="script">l</mi></math> is defined by <math alttext="3 y plus 12 x equals 5"><mn>3</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>12</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn></math>. Line <math alttext="n"><mi>n</mi>
