ds\"><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>5</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac></math>. Thus, the slope of line&nbsp;<math alttext=\"script l\"><mi mathvariant=\"script\">l</mi></math> in the <em>xy</em>-plane is <math alttext=\"negative 4\"><mrow>\n<mo>-</mo>\n<mn>4</mn>\n</mrow>\n</math>. Since line <math alttext=\"n\"><mi>n</mi>\n</math> is perpendicular to line <math alttext=\"script l\"><mi mathvariant=\"script\">l</mi></math> in the <em>xy</em>-plane, the slope of line <math alttext=\"n\"><mi>n</mi>\n</math> is the negative reciprocal of the slope of line <math alttext=\"script l\"><mi mathvariant=\"script\">l</mi></math>. The negative reciprocal of <math alttext=\"negative 4\"><mrow>\n<mo>-</mo>\n<mn>4</mn>\n</mrow>\n</math> is <math alttext=\"minus StartFraction 1 Over left parenthesis negative 4 right parenthesis EndFraction equals one fourth\"><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mfenced><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></mfenced></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac></math>. Note that 1/4 and .25 are examples of ways to enter a correct answer.</p>","externalid":"2b8c0dff-e373-422a-a150-3f281e461330","answerOptions":[],"correct_answer":["0.25","1/4"]},"createDate":1743430554981,"updateDate":1743430554981}$SATQ$::jsonb, 1743430554981, 1743430554981),
