$SATQ$, $SATQ$<p class="stem_paragraph ">The table above shows the coordinates of three points on a line in the <span class="italic ">xy</span>-plane, where <span class="italic">k</span> and <span class="italic">n</span> are constants. If the slope of the line is 2, what is the value of <span class="math_expression "><span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/0366d965/img_000_8d406142.png" alt="k plus n"></span>&nbsp;</span>?</p>
$SATQ$, NULL, $SATQ$["30"]$SATQ$::jsonb, NULL, $SATQ$<p>The correct answer is 30. The slope of a line can be found by using the slope formula, <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/0366d965/img_001_32dd89fa.png" alt="the fraction with numerator y sub 2 minus y sub 1, and denominator x sub 2 minus x sub 1, end fraction"></span>. It&rsquo;s given that the slope of the line is 2; therefore, <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/0366d965/img_002_437015dd.png" alt="the fraction with numerator y sub 2 minus y sub 1, and denominator x sub 2 minus x sub 1, end fraction, equals 2"></span>. According to the table, the points <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/0366d965/img_003_32d9a07d.png" alt="with coordinates 3 comma 7"></span> and <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/0366d965/img_004_acd09402.png" alt="with coordinates k comma 11"></span> lie on the line. Substituting the coordinates of these points into the equation gives <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/0366d965/img_005_13488e82.png" alt="the fraction with numerator 11 minus 7, and denominator k minus 3, end fraction, equals 2"></span>. Multiplying both sides of this equation by <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/0366d965/img_006_f21441a7.png" alt="k minus 3 "></span> gives <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/0366d965/img_007_56b5f689.png" alt="11 minus 7, equals, 2 times, open parenthesis, k minus 3, close parenthesis"></span>, or <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/0366d965/img_008_0e4a7ccb.png" alt="11 minus 7, equals, 2 k minus 6"></span>. Solving for <span class="italic">k</span> gives <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/0366d965/img_009_6374fc88.png" alt="k equals 5"></span>. According to the table, the points <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/0366d965/img_010_32d9a07d.png" alt="with coordinates 3 comma 7"></span> and <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/0366d965/img_011_fcb168bd.png" alt="with coordinates 12 comma n"></span> also lie on the line. Substituting the coordinates of these points into <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/0366d965/img_012_437015dd.png" alt="the fraction with numerator y sub 2 minus y sub 1, and denominator x sub 2 minus x sub 1, end fraction, equals 2 "></span> gives <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/0366d965/img_013_02561def.png" alt="the fraction with numerator n minus 7, and denominator 12 minus 3, end fraction, equals 2"></span>. Solving for <span class="italic">n</span> gives <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/0366d965/img_014_7f1e6edc.png" alt="n equals 25"></span>. Therefore, <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/0366d965/img_015_2b166851.png" alt="k plus n, equals, 5 plus 25"></span>, or 30.</p>
