    ($SATQ$038d87d7$SATQ$, $SATQ$4e5c1cee-ad79-4a5a-8828-24762395ae21$SATQ$::uuid, $SATQ$2e2e11d6-2774-4c37-a214-27fdf83d488e$SATQ$::uuid, NULL, $SATQ$qbank$SATQ$, $SATQ$SAT$SATQ$, 2, $SATQ$Math$SATQ$, $SATQ$Algebra$SATQ$, $SATQ$H$SATQ$, $SATQ$H.C.$SATQ$, $SATQ$Linear equations in two variables$SATQ$, $SATQ$M$SATQ$, 5, $SATQ$mcq$SATQ$, NULL, $SATQ$<p>A neighborhood consists of a <math alttext="2"><mn>2</mn>
</math>-hectare park and a <math alttext="35"><mn>35</mn>
</math>-hectare residential area. The total number of trees in the neighborhood is <math alttext="3,934"><mn>3,934</mn>
</math>. The equation <math alttext="2 x plus 35 y equals 3,934"><mrow>
	<mrow>
		<mrow>
			<mn>2</mn>
			<mi>x</mi>
		</mrow>
		<mo>+</mo>
		<mrow>
			<mn>35</mn>
			<mi>y</mi>
		</mrow>
	</mrow>
	<mo>=</mo>
	<mn>3,934</mn>
</mrow>
</math> represents this situation. Which of the following is the best interpretation of <em>x</em> in this context?</p>$SATQ$, $SATQ$[{"id":"151f1193-b35c-43cc-9f93-76376a7f6868","content":"<p>The average number of trees per hectare in the park</p>"},{"id":"2182c3aa-4017-4535-954a-88b94115a954","content":"<p>The average number of trees per hectare in the residential area</p>"},{"id":"53c518df-4e68-4ca2-b38a-738d8486f02b","content":"<p>The total number of trees in the park</p>"},{"id":"f8503a99-4789-4cee-9e6d-5aca6fed46dd","content":"<p>The total number of trees in the residential area</p>"}]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["A"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["151f1193-b35c-43cc-9f93-76376a7f6868"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$<p>Choice A is correct. It's given that a neighborhood consists of a <math alttext="2"><mn>2</mn>
</math>-hectare park and a <math alttext="35"><mn>35</mn>
</math>-hectare residential area and that the total number of trees in the neighborhood is <math alttext="3,934"><mn>3,934</mn>
</math>. It's also given that the equation <math alttext="2 x plus 35 y equals 3,934"><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>35</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3,934</mn></math> represents this situation. Since the total number of trees for a given area can be determined by taking the number of hectares times the average number of trees per hectare, this must mean that the terms <math alttext="2 x"><mrow>
	<mn>2</mn>
	<mi>x</mi>
</mrow>
</math> and <math alttext="35 y"><mrow>
	<mn>35</mn>
	<mi>y</mi>
</mrow>
</math> correspond to the number of trees in the park and in the residential area, respectively. Since <math alttext="2 x"><mrow>
	<mn>2</mn>
	<mi>x</mi>
</mrow>
</math> corresponds to the number of trees in the park, and <math alttext="2"><mn>2</mn>
</math> is the size of the park, in hectares, <math alttext="x"><mi>x</mi>
</math> must represent the average number of trees per hectare in the park.</p>
